WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:08.334
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Here is a standard pack of playing cards:

2
00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:20.996
fifty-two cards, four suits – spades, clubs, diamonds, hearts – twelve picture cards, two jokers.

3
00:00:21.551 --> 00:00:29.161
Most people are familiar with these cards. But what do you know about their history and their uses?

4
00:00:29.731 --> 00:00:36.601
The first playing cards originated in Asia, probably in China in the ninth century.

5
00:00:37.156 --> 00:00:43.318
Between the ninth and the fourteenth centuries they travelled west across the world,

6
00:00:43.456 --> 00:00:47.985
through India, Persia, and Egypt, to Europe.

7
00:00:49.187 --> 00:00:53.300
The early cards looked different from the ones we know today,

8
00:00:53.469 --> 00:01:03.451
and the suits were different in different countries, for example, cups, swords, leaves, bells, and roses.

9
00:01:04.237 --> 00:01:11.462
The picture cards were all male figures, the king, the jack, and a soldier on a horse.

10
00:01:12.309 --> 00:01:20.520
From the sixteenth century, the French pack of fifty-two cards that we know today became the most common.

11
00:01:20.689 --> 00:01:29.223
Its design was simple and therefore cheap to print. Why are there fifty-two cards?

12
00:01:29.393 --> 00:01:33.798
And why four suits…and twelve picture cards?

13
00:01:34.245 --> 00:01:45.059
No one knows for sure, but an interesting theory is that the fifty-two cards represent the fifty-two weeks in a year,

14
00:01:45.521 --> 00:01:53.039
the four suits represent the four seasons (spring, summer, autumn, and winter),

15
00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:59.108
and the twelve picture cards represent the twelve months of the year.

16
00:01:59.724 --> 00:02:08.197
The highest picture card is the king. On the king card, the king always has a sword or an axe.

17
00:02:08.381 --> 00:02:17.347
The kings also always have moustaches, except for the king of hearts, who sometimes doesn’t have one.

18
00:02:17.932 --> 00:02:26.436
The second highest picture card is the queen. The French introduced the queen instead of the soldier on a horse.

19
00:02:26.929 --> 00:02:31.673
On the queen card, the queen always has a flower in her hand.

20
00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:38.436
In English packs of cards, the jack was originally called the knave.

21
00:02:38.744 --> 00:02:44.551
However, because the initials of the picture cards appear in the corner of each card,

22
00:02:44.598 --> 00:02:50.282
and there was already a ‘K’ for ‘king’, knave became ‘jack’.

23
00:02:51.607 --> 00:02:56.397
The jokers were first added to the pack in the eighteen fifties.

24
00:02:56.721 --> 00:03:03.930
They soon became a standard part of the pack, and in some games they are ‘wild cards’, that is,

25
00:03:03.976 --> 00:03:10.138
they can be any card. Playing cards quickly became very popular.

26
00:03:10.539 --> 00:03:15.052
This was because previously most games were for two players.

27
00:03:15.407 --> 00:03:23.047
Card games were ideal for lots of different numbers of players, and were especially popular with women.

28
00:03:23.664 --> 00:03:31.011
The international fifty-two-card pack is still very popular all over the world with people of all ages:

29
00:03:31.181 --> 00:03:39.777
easy children’s games, games for one person, and serious games like Bridge or Canasta.

30
00:03:40.485 --> 00:03:44.121
But playing cards are not only for games.

31
00:03:44.521 --> 00:03:49.851
Although there are special fortune-telling card packs, like tarot cards,

32
00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:59.202
the standard pack was also a very popular way to tell people’s fortune in the eighteenth, nineteenth, and twentieth centuries.

33
00:03:59.849 --> 00:04:07.536
The four suits represent four themes: spades are about challenges or difficulties,

34
00:04:07.982 --> 00:04:18.026
hearts are about feelings and relationships, clubs are about positive things, diamonds are about money.

35
00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:23.079
Each number and picture card also has a special meaning.

36
00:04:23.402 --> 00:04:28.363
You can have all sorts of fun with cards in many different ways.